source	Plato, Euthydemus 275d-276c, tr. B. Jowett
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 1598, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1598
class	equivocation
word	learn
fault	"learn" is acquiring knowledge one lacks in the first argument (so the unlearned learn) and understanding what one is told in the second (so the wise learn): each conclusion holds only in its own sense, and they do not contradict each other
reference	Plato, Euthydemus 277e-278b (Socrates names the two senses); Aristotle, Sophistical Refutations 4, 165b32
